(4154152, 589614, 34562, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by BeeCee:</b></div><hr/><i> Don''t let it break you. This is still an absolutely STUNNING image that should be on DPPrints.  Those 9 faves should be worth as much as a virtual ribbon, no? :) </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>Yeah you''re probably right but it still is a blast to the face either way. Might be kind of stupid but after moving to NY and then having to repack all your stuff 2 1/2 weeks later and moving again, watching your first ribbon develop actually helped some of the pain of what I was going through. There where only 2 days left of voting and I didn''t feel that there was ever a chance of being asked for the original on such a simply straight forward picture. But all 5 of the top images are asked to validate- that should be better publicized then. And yes I am just a bit sulky about that. I don''t cheat and this makes me feel like I was suspected of that. I could of easily pulled the original off the desktop and had it on my laptop ready to send off if I''d known that top 5 where asked to validate.</td>', 'Originally posted by BeeCee: Don''t let it break you. This is still an absolutely STUNNING image that should be on DPPrints.  Those 9 faves should be worth as much as a virtual ribbon, no? :)   Yeah you''re probably right but it still is a blast to the face either way. Might be kind of stupid but after moving to NY and then having to repack all your stuff 2 1/2 weeks later and moving again, watching your first ribbon develop actually helped some of the pain of what I was going through. There where only 2 days left of voting and I didn''t feel that there was ever a chance of being asked for the original on such a simply straight forward picture. But all 5 of the top images are asked to validate- that should be better publicized then. And yes I am just a bit sulky about that. I don''t cheat and this makes me feel like I was suspected of that. I could of easily pulled the original off the desktop and had it on my laptop ready to send off if I''d known that top 5 where asked to validate.', '2007-10-09 11:12:02.000000', NULL, 0),
(4154236, 591028, 29490, '<td valign="top">Up to a ribbon! - congrats manny!</td>', 'Up to a ribbon! - congrats manny!', '2007-10-09 11:47:32.000000', NULL, 0),
(4154367, 591574, 30861, '<td valign="top">Wonderful shot, one of my top picks this challenge. Almost a third of the votes are 7 and higher, which is a lot for a 5.7 image; a lot of the voters felt this was exceptional. Fie on the nay-sayers!</td>', 'Wonderful shot, one of my top picks this challenge. Almost a third of the votes are 7 and higher, which is a lot for a 5.7 image; a lot of the voters felt this was exceptional. Fie on the nay-sayers!', '2007-10-09 12:41:40.000000', NULL, 0),
(4154714, 589614, 61961, '<td valign="top">James, it''s a shame the image was disqualified.  It can feel personal, but don''t believe it.  It has happened "unfairly" to many others before you and will no doubt continue to happen.  There are so many rules to pay attention to, one pretty much has to be around awhile to follow them.<br/> <br/>There is btw an option to submit a request for validation along with your entry, or anyway sometime before the challenge ends.  Unfortunately, again, you would have to be around awhile to realize that might be necessary!<br/> <br/>Great photo, by the way.  I''ve also enjoyed checking out your portfolio.<br/> <br/>Cheers,<br/> - Larry in NYC</td>', 'James, it''s a shame the image was disqualified.  It can feel personal, but don''t believe it.  It has happened "unfairly" to many others before you and will no doubt continue to happen.  There are so many rules to pay attention to, one pretty much has to be around awhile to follow them. There is btw an option to submit a request for validation along with your entry, or anyway sometime before the challenge ends.  Unfortunately, again, you would have to be around awhile to realize that might be necessary! Great photo, by the way.  I''ve also enjoyed checking out your portfolio. Cheers, - Larry in NYC', '2007-10-09 15:24:18.000000', NULL, 0),
(4154830, 591028, 34562, '<td valign="top">Though it stinks to be bumped out and DQ''ed it''s nice to see another great photo move up to a ribbon. Cheers. Very captivating image.</td>', 'Though it stinks to be bumped out and DQ''ed it''s nice to see another great photo move up to a ribbon. Cheers. Very captivating image.', '2007-10-09 16:36:17.000000', NULL, 0),
(4154843, 589950, 34562, '<td valign="top">Though I hate to get DQ''ed it doesn''t bother me a bit to see such a great image get bumped up a notch. Congrats to a fine photo.</td>', 'Though I hate to get DQ''ed it doesn''t bother me a bit to see such a great image get bumped up a notch. Congrats to a fine photo.', '2007-10-09 16:51:36.000000', NULL, 0),
(4155020, 590023, 14414, '<td valign="top">very graphic image. a lot of noise ninja, but its alright - it fits the style. Nice composition.</td>', 'very graphic image. a lot of noise ninja, but its alright - it fits the style. Nice composition.', '2007-10-09 18:34:36.000000', NULL, 0),
(4155134, 591028, 26475, '<td valign="top">The premise is really good, and the woman is gorgeous, but there''s something offsetting about the photo. The "rain" looks like it''s droplets sprayed on a sheet of plexiglass and positioned in front of the woman. The focus is on the droplets and not the woman, which draws the eye away. Additionally, there looks like there''s some sort of haze or reflection in front of her on the top half of the photo. <br/> <br/>All in all, good effort, but It could be better.<br/> <br/>MO.<br/> <br/>Steph<br/> <br/>I want to add that I''ve always loved your work - I think you''re an exceptional photographer, but this one just looked a bit forced.<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2007-10-09 18:37:23.</i></td>', 'The premise is really good, and the woman is gorgeous, but there''s something offsetting about the photo. The "rain" looks like it''s droplets sprayed on a sheet of plexiglass and positioned in front of the woman. The focus is on the droplets and not the woman, which draws the eye away. Additionally, there looks like there''s some sort of haze or reflection in front of her on the top half of the photo.  All in all, good effort, but It could be better. MO. Steph I want to add that I''ve always loved your work - I think you''re an exceptional photographer, but this one just looked a bit forced.', '2007-10-09 19:35:39.000000', '2007-10-09 19:37:23.000000', 0),
